[1m[31mE               The `Example` object is immutable and not connected to any directory.[0m
[1m[31mE               A temporary directory is only created when you call a `run_*` method.[0m
[1m[31mE               The result of the `run_*` method is always a new `Example` object with the updated files.[0m
[1m[31mE               This means that you can create an `Example` and call the `run_*` methods on it in any order you want, with the arguments that are useful for your test case.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               This allows for more complex tests where you create one example and perform multiple test runs on it. Every test run will work on the changed files from the previous one.[0m
