[1m[31mE               The approval of this type of changes is easier, because the update category assures that the value has not changed.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               The goal of inline-snapshot is to generate the values for you in the correct format so that no manual editing is required.[0m
[1m[31mE               This improves your productivity and saves time.[0m
[1m[31mE               Keep in mind that any changes you make to your snapshots will likely need to be redone if your program's behaviour (and expected values) change.[0m
[1m[31mE               Inline-snapshot uses the *update* category to let you know when it has a different opinion than you about how the code should look.[0m
[1m[31mE               You can agree with inline-snapshot and accept the changes or you can use one of the following options to tell inline-snapshot what the code should look like:[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               1. change the `__repr__` implementation of your object or use [customize repr](customize_repr.md) if the class is not part of your codebase.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               2. define a [format-command](configuration.md#format-command) if another tool has a different opinion about how your code should look. Inline-snapshot will apply this formatting before reporting an update.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               3. inline-snapshot manages everything within `snapshot(...)`, but you can take control by using [Is()](eq_snapshot.md#is) in cases where you want to use custom code (like local variables) in your snapshots.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               4. you can also open an [issue](https://github.com/15r10nk/inline-snapshot/issues?q=is%3Aissue%20state%3Aopen%20label%3Aupdate_related) if you have a specific problem with the way inline-snapshot generates the code.[0m
[1m[31mE               [0m
[1m[31mE               !!! note[0m
[1m[31mE                   [#177](https://github.com/15r10nk/inline-snapshot/issues/177) will give the developer more control about how snapshots are created. *update* will then become much more useful.[0m

